  "prefLabel": "Plc 502.15 Protected health information (PHI)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 502.15 “Protected health information (PHI)” means any information in a medical record or designated record set that can be used to identify an individual and that was created, used, or disclosed in the course of obtaining or providing a health care service such as diagnosis or treatment.\n\nSource. #13971, eff 7-1-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc500.html"
